(5820160, 847253, 66384, '<td valign="top">The processing seems a little heavy handed. I like the subject and the composition though.</td>', 'The processing seems a little heavy handed. I like the subject and the composition though.', '2010-01-20 18:00:44.000000', NULL, 1),
(5820180, 847565, 66384, '<td valign="top">You will score higher, if you size your photo better (there is a tutorial on how to do it) and if you adjust it to reduce the haze and increase the clarity. A levels adjustment, or even an auto adjustment, would help enormously.</td>', 'You will score higher, if you size your photo better (there is a tutorial on how to do it) and if you adjust it to reduce the haze and increase the clarity. A levels adjustment, or even an auto adjustment, would help enormously.', '2010-01-20 18:11:24.000000', NULL, 1),
(5820186, 847135, 66384, '<td valign="top">I don''t think a picture of a picture of a person meets the challenge of an inanimate object.</td>', 'I don''t think a picture of a picture of a person meets the challenge of an inanimate object.', '2010-01-20 18:15:21.000000', NULL, 1),
(5820195, 847660, 66384, '<td valign="top">Well done. Love the colors and the clean lines of this.</td>', 'Well done. Love the colors and the clean lines of this.', '2010-01-20 18:18:59.000000', NULL, 1),
(5820467, 847680, 63918, '<td valign="top">I REALLY like the shot, but it doesn''t quite hit the assignment...to me anyway...something about the eyes.</td>', 'I REALLY like the shot, but it doesn''t quite hit the assignment...to me anyway...something about the eyes.', '2010-01-20 21:22:12.000000', NULL, 1),
(5820486, 847680, 43463, '<td valign="top">Life''s a beach when you have a bucketful of fun:-) Nice use of leading lines that draws our eye to the vanishing point off into the horizon. As we ''walk'' there with our eyes, we spy this shovels and sand pail to grab as we stroll down the the beach. The handle smile on the bucket invokes a sense of a happy play day. My only plaint with this face is that it *could* be stronger - some may have trouble seeing the eyes and smile at first glance. A nose would have made the emphasis of the face stronger - perhaps a small sifter or very small rake hanging over the side to serve as a nose would have worked. Still very creative image and well done - 8</td>', 'Life''s a beach when you have a bucketful of fun:-) Nice use of leading lines that draws our eye to the vanishing point off into the horizon. As we ''walk'' there with our eyes, we spy this shovels and sand pail to grab as we stroll down the the beach. The handle smile on the bucket invokes a sense of a happy play day. My only plaint with this face is that it *could* be stronger - some may have trouble seeing the eyes and smile at first glance. A nose would have made the emphasis of the face stronger - perhaps a small sifter or very small rake hanging over the side to serve as a nose would have worked. Still very creative image and well done - 8', '2010-01-20 21:43:45.000000', NULL, 1),
(5820502, 847522, 43463, '<td valign="top">April was nice and clean - with a hint of May flowers as she broke into a smile and reached for the towel:-)<br/> <br/>Wow, look at the image details from the red towel to the water drops seen on the white walls and the chrome smile. Love the addition of the red towel for it brings color to what would otherwise be a stark image composed of just silver and whites. Plus it adds to the personification of the shower "person" finishing up and getting ready to towel off. Great work here!</td>', 'April was nice and clean - with a hint of May flowers as she broke into a smile and reached for the towel:-) Wow, look at the image details from the red towel to the water drops seen on the white walls and the chrome smile. Love the addition of the red towel for it brings color to what would otherwise be a stark image composed of just silver and whites. Plus it adds to the personification of the shower "person" finishing up and getting ready to towel off. Great work here!', '2010-01-20 21:53:51.000000', NULL, 1),
(5820508, 847487, 67585, '<td valign="top">This is fantastic, very nice editing as well. TEN from me...</td>', 'This is fantastic, very nice editing as well. TEN from me...', '2010-01-20 22:00:49.000000', NULL, 1),
(5820511, 847636, 43463, '<td valign="top">The opposite of Oscar the Grouch - Grady the Grater sings, "I looovvvve cheese, whether its sliced, or grated or cubed. Soft-ripened, blue-veined, or processed, I looooooovvvveee cheese!"<br/> <br/>Um, yeah, boy that was cheesy:-) Okay, great find - love the smiling expression on this cheese grater. Composition and clarity is wonderful. Lighting is good but I wish that deep shadow behind was not so evident. Moving the grater further away from the backdrop would have avoided it casting the shadow on the ''wall''. Nonetheless it is not too distracting that it draws away from the main subject. Great job!</td>', 'The opposite of Oscar the Grouch - Grady the Grater sings, "I looovvvve cheese, whether its sliced, or grated or cubed. Soft-ripened, blue-veined, or processed, I looooooovvvveee cheese!" Um, yeah, boy that was cheesy:-) Okay, great find - love the smiling expression on this cheese grater. Composition and clarity is wonderful. Lighting is good but I wish that deep shadow behind was not so evident. Moving the grater further away from the backdrop would have avoided it casting the shadow on the ''wall''. Nonetheless it is not too distracting that it draws away from the main subject. Great job!', '2010-01-20 22:02:27.000000', NULL, 1),
(5820513, 847128, 67585, '<td valign="top">Funny stuff! Creative/Humorous idea!</td>', 'Funny stuff! Creative/Humorous idea!', '2010-01-20 22:03:43.000000', NULL, 1),
(5820532, 847303, 43463, '<td valign="top">I have enough trouble looking at things right side up to see faces but you turn things upside down to get us to see into a topsy-turvy world:-) Very creative work that uses the whole room to make the smiling face! Love how the chairs act as the eyebrows or eyelashes (whichever way you want to look at it) for the circular eyes of the clock and the oval picture. BW was most definatly the best choice to go with for the (most likely opposing) colors of all teh objects would have been distracting. The smiling face is much more recognizable this way. Not to keen on the title, but I can see what you are alluding to with the teeth as the window panes and the foliage outside as the ''food'' stuck on the teeth.</td>', 'I have enough trouble looking at things right side up to see faces but you turn things upside down to get us to see into a topsy-turvy world:-) Very creative work that uses the whole room to make the smiling face! Love how the chairs act as the eyebrows or eyelashes (whichever way you want to look at it) for the circular eyes of the clock and the oval picture. BW was most definatly the best choice to go with for the (most likely opposing) colors of all teh objects would have been distracting. The smiling face is much more recognizable this way. Not to keen on the title, but I can see what you are alluding to with the teeth as the window panes and the foliage outside as the ''food'' stuck on the teeth.', '2010-01-20 22:15:38.000000', NULL, 1),
(5820537, 847389, 15711, '<td valign="top">Now I''ll hear that "Somebody''s watching me" all night LOL</td>', 'Now I''ll hear that "Somebody''s watching me" all night LOL', '2010-01-20 22:17:05.000000', NULL, 1),
