(5831858, 847714, 110023, '<td valign="top">For those who are curious as to the reason for the curb chain with the snaffle...   :)<br/> <br/>This combination had to be used with a young filly we were breaking last Spring. She had a bad tendency to throw her head and play with the bit. We wanted to bit her as gentle as possible so we went with this snaffle. In order to keep her from flipping it, we added a curb chain. Of course a curb chain has no effect on the chin with a snaffle but it did work well to keep this bit in place. I''ve also done this a lot also with my hunter jumper headstalls but with a leather curb instead.<br/> <br/>Getting started...<br/><img alt="'' . substr(''//i230.photobucket.com/albums/ee73/gemini_6369/Lacie5-1-1.jpg'', strrpos(''//i230.photobucket.com/albums/ee73/gemini_6369/Lacie5-1-1.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//i230.photobucket.com/albums/ee73/gemini_6369/Lacie5-1-1.jpg"/> <br/> <br/>Here she is being ridden for the first time by me...<br/><img alt="'' . substr(''//i230.photobucket.com/albums/ee73/gemini_6369/Lacie1-1.jpg'', strrpos(''//i230.photobucket.com/albums/ee73/gemini_6369/Lacie1-1.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//i230.photobucket.com/albums/ee73/gemini_6369/Lacie1-1.jpg"/></td>', 'For those who are curious as to the reason for the curb chain with the snaffle...   :) This combination had to be used with a young filly we were breaking last Spring. She had a bad tendency to throw her head and play with the bit. We wanted to bit her as gentle as possible so we went with this snaffle. In order to keep her from flipping it, we added a curb chain. Of course a curb chain has no effect on the chin with a snaffle but it did work well to keep this bit in place. I''ve also done this a lot also with my hunter jumper headstalls but with a leather curb instead. Getting started...  Here she is being ridden for the first time by me...', '2010-01-25 10:42:44.000000', NULL, 0),
