(5833401, 847492, 103142, '<td valign="top">Good day! You''re the recipient of a "critique club" critique! So feel free to take this with a grain of salt :D<br/> <br/>First Impression: I wonder how many of your lower votes were from people who just don''t like fish-eye shots. There does seem to be strong reactions to them. Personally, I don''t care much for fish-eyes, however, I find this one intriguing. The face seemed difficult to find, at first.<br/> <br/>Composition: I like the composition. Two small things, however: the image seems a tad tilted to the right. Have you tried rotating it slightly to the left? (small point, but might be a little better.) Second, I find the tables in the lower left hand corner draw my eye. I don''t think there''s much you could do about it, but I''d be curious if you stepped back a bit and didn''t cut through them whether it would lessen their importance. Again, very small point, but you chose a good POV!<br/> <br/>Subject: Not sure about the quality of the face. It was a little hard to see, and pretty small in the picture (the one I found, that is). I think this hurt you with some people. Once found, however, it is interesting. The curving portion seems like arms wrapping around, and thus it was a very good choice of title!<br/> <br/>Technical: The technicals look good to me. The only change that I''d consider is perhaps bringing out the blues in the sky. Otherwise, I think it''s quite nice.<br/> <br/>Final thoughts: Nice idea, interesting shot. I think you might have been hit by the speed voters that didn''t want to take time to find the face.</td>', 'Good day! You''re the recipient of a "critique club" critique! So feel free to take this with a grain of salt :D First Impression: I wonder how many of your lower votes were from people who just don''t like fish-eye shots. There does seem to be strong reactions to them. Personally, I don''t care much for fish-eyes, however, I find this one intriguing. The face seemed difficult to find, at first. Composition: I like the composition. Two small things, however: the image seems a tad tilted to the right. Have you tried rotating it slightly to the left? (small point, but might be a little better.) Second, I find the tables in the lower left hand corner draw my eye. I don''t think there''s much you could do about it, but I''d be curious if you stepped back a bit and didn''t cut through them whether it would lessen their importance. Again, very small point, but you chose a good POV! Subject: Not sure about the quality of the face. It was a little hard to see, and pretty small in the picture (the one I found, that is). I think this hurt you with some people. Once found, however, it is interesting. The curving portion seems like arms wrapping around, and thus it was a very good choice of title! Technical: The technicals look good to me. The only change that I''d consider is perhaps bringing out the blues in the sky. Otherwise, I think it''s quite nice. Final thoughts: Nice idea, interesting shot. I think you might have been hit by the speed voters that didn''t want to take time to find the face.', '2010-01-25 19:47:32.000000', NULL, 0),
(5833455, 847320, 112107, '<td valign="top"><b>Greetings from the Critique Club</b> ;)<br/> <br/><b>Artistic Merit</b> <br/>Pros: <br/>* The less than obvious head on view of the subject catching the reflections creates a good sense of depth.<br/>* Good choice of subject placement with the negative space on the right place (with the subject look making him part of the picture).<br/>* There are two implicit very strong circular lines that feed each other keeping the viewer''s attention.<br/>* The color contrasts very well with the monotone areas.<br/> <br/>Cons: <br/>* The crop is too tight leaving no place for the subject to "breathe".<br/>* As pointed before, the background (where in focus) is competing for attention even though it''s almost featureless.<br/> <br/><b>Technical Merit</b> <br/>Pros: <br/>* The focus is spot on.<br/>* The photo is well exposed.<br/> <br/>Cons: <br/>* There isn''t enough DOF on the subject''s frame.<br/>* There is too much DOF on the background.<br/>* The photo lacks contrast and saturation for my taste, lowering the grey point would help both. Lowering the black point could also help strenghtening the blacks in the circular frame.<br/>* Lightening is slightly uneven even though you almost managed to kill all reflections.<br/> <br/><b>Emotional Merit</b> <br/>Pros:<br/>* This is an funny and original picture.<br/> <br/>Cons: <br/>* The (angry) eyes and a (smiling) mouth convey contradictory feelings.<br/> <br/><b>Result</b> <br/>I guess this picture was let down mostly by the technical aspects (which are well within your reach, judging by your portfolio) and the tight crop. AFAIK originality (where it could have gathered some points) this was a tough challenge prone to have strong competition. In a more objectively themed challenge, I believe it would have performed in the upper half of the pack.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2010-01-25 20:32:49.</i></td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club ;) Artistic Merit Pros: * The less than obvious head on view of the subject catching the reflections creates a good sense of depth.* Good choice of subject placement with the negative space on the right place (with the subject look making him part of the picture).* There are two implicit very strong circular lines that feed each other keeping the viewer''s attention.* The color contrasts very well with the monotone areas. Cons: * The crop is too tight leaving no place for the subject to "breathe".* As pointed before, the background (where in focus) is competing for attention even though it''s almost featureless. Technical Merit Pros: * The focus is spot on.* The photo is well exposed. Cons: * There isn''t enough DOF on the subject''s frame.* There is too much DOF on the background.* The photo lacks contrast and saturation for my taste, lowering the grey point would help both. Lowering the black point could also help strenghtening the blacks in the circular frame.* Lightening is slightly uneven even though you almost managed to kill all reflections. Emotional Merit Pros:* This is an funny and original picture. Cons: * The (angry) eyes and a (smiling) mouth convey contradictory feelings. Result I guess this picture was let down mostly by the technical aspects (which are well within your reach, judging by your portfolio) and the tight crop. AFAIK originality (where it could have gathered some points) this was a tough challenge prone to have strong competition. In a more objectively themed challenge, I believe it would have performed in the upper half of the pack.', '2010-01-25 20:09:53.000000', '2010-01-25 20:32:49.000000', 0),
